<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- Sedation-buildup hediff carried by the UMW_Opiated coating (UMW_Stab_Tranq's additionalHediffs).
       Accumulates like Core's ToxicBuildup (Pawn_HealthTracker.PostApplyDamage applies additionalHediffs on
       every Thing.TakeDamage; base Hediff.TryMergeWith then merges same-def whole-body hediffs, SUMMING
       severity) — see the on-hit-effects note in CLAUDE.md.

       Why a custom hediff, not vanilla Anesthetic: Anesthetic is authored for the DECAY direction, not
       buildup. Its stage 0 is labelled "wearing off" (reads backwards while severity is climbing toward a
       downed state), its HediffCompProperties_Disappears (45000~120000t) wholesale-removes the merged
       instance on a timer rolled once at first application (so a second dose doesn't reliably extend
       captivity), its 0/0.6/0.8 stage thresholds give a lopsided cadence for our faster proc rate, and its
       -0.8/day decay is surgery pacing (a patient recovers from anesthesia in minutes, not the hours a
       capture window needs). We clone its capMods onto a buildup-shaped ladder instead: no Disappears comp
       (a straight SeverityPerDay decay handles wake-up), and thresholds re-tuned for our per-hit severity
       (see UMW_Stab_Tranq).

       Deliberately OMITS canApplyDodChanceForCapacityChanges (default false): a sedation-down must NEVER
       roll instant-death via a capacity-loss death check — that's the whole point of a non-lethal capture
       coating. Contrast Core's ToxicBuildup, which sets this true (poisoning IS meant to be able to kill);
       the omission here is deliberate, not an oversight.

       Pacing math (size-1, unarmored target, see UMW_Stab_Tranq for the per-hit severity derivation):
       ~0.20 severity/hit -> a stage-up roughly every 1.75 landed hits -> downed (0.7 threshold) after
       3-4 hits. Wake-up: severity caps at 1.0, decays at -1.5/day, so it crosses back below the 0.7 downed
       threshold in about 4.8 hours from a full dose - a capture window, not a hospital stay.

       Tuning knobs if playtest runs hot/cold: UMW_Stab_Tranq's severityPerDamageDealt (+-0.01 is
       roughly +-15% pacing), this def's SeverityPerDay decay rate, and the stage thresholds below. -->
  <HediffDef>
    <defName>UMW_SedativeBuildup</defName>
    <label>sedative buildup</label>
    <description>A fast-acting sedative building up in the bloodstream. At high levels it renders the creature unconscious.</description>
    <hediffClass>HediffWithComps</hediffClass>
    <maxSeverity>1</maxSeverity>
    <comps>
      <li Class="HediffCompProperties_SeverityPerDay">
        <severityPerDay>-1.5</severityPerDay>
      </li>
    </comps>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>dosed</label>
        <painFactor>0.95</painFactor>
        <capMods>
          <li>
            <capacity>Consciousness</capacity>
            <setMax>0.9</setMax>
          </li>
          <li>
            <capacity>Moving</capacity>
            <offset>-0.05</offset>
          </li>
          <li>
            <capacity>Manipulation</capacity>
            <offset>-0.1</offset>
          </li>
        </capMods>
      </li>
      <li>
        <minSeverity>0.35</minSeverity>
        <label>woozy</label>
        <painFactor>0.8</painFactor>
        <capMods>
          <li>
            <capacity>Consciousness</capacity>
            <setMax>0.7</setMax>
          </li>
          <li>
            <capacity>Moving</capacity>
            <offset>-0.2</offset>
          </li>
          <li>
            <capacity>Manipulation</capacity>
            <offset>-0.2</offset>
          </li>
          <li>
            <capacity>Talking</capacity>
            <offset>-0.2</offset>
          </li>
          <li>
            <capacity>Sight</capacity>
            <offset>-0.15</offset>
          </li>
        </capMods>
      </li>
      <li>
        <minSeverity>0.7</minSeverity>
        <label>sedated</label>
        <painFactor>0</painFactor>
        <capMods>
          <li>
            <capacity>Consciousness</capacity>
            <setMax>0.01</setMax>
          </li>
        </capMods>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </HediffDef>

</Defs>
